# UI conventions

## Two visual systems

1. **App chrome** (sidebar, settings, gallery, sheets): shadcn **base-nova** + `@base-ui/react`, semantic tokens, `cn()` from `lib/utils.ts`. Follow `.agents/skills/shadcn/` when adding/editing shadcn components (`pnpm dlx shadcn@latest`).
2. **Workflow nodes / canvas**: custom dark design system in `app/globals.css` (`.node-card`, handles, accents). Prefer those classes over forcing shadcn Cards inside nodes.

## Canvas look (established)

- Page/canvas background ~`#0B0E14` / black; nodes `#141820`.
- Accents per node type from `NODE_META` (teal image gen, green text, orange image input, etc.).
- Icons: `lucide-react`. Motion: `motion/react` where already used.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — generic card inside a node
<Card><CardContent>...</CardContent></Card>

// ✅ GOOD — node shell
<div className="node-card">...</div>
```

## shadcn / Base UI

- Compose existing `components/ui/*` before inventing primitives.
- Base UI uses `render` (not Radix `asChild`) for custom triggers — see shadcn skill `base-vs-radix.md`.
- Prefer `flex` + `gap-*` over `space-y-*`. Use `cn()` for conditional classes.
- Toasts in this app use the custom `Toaster` / store toasts — do not assume `sonner` is wired unless already imported.

## Client boundaries

- Interactive canvas, modals, sidebar controls: `"use client"`.
- Keep server Components in `app/` layouts/pages when they only read cookies/metadata.
